number|title|condition|evidence|remediation|limitation|attack|nist|nist_rationale|sources|severity
001|A lower-trust GPO editor controls domain controllers feeding the tenant|An unapproved principal can change effective execution or administrative policy on domain controllers in a forest that supplies assessed hybrid identities.|GPO and SYSVOL effective write; resultant DC policy; setting semantics; forest-to-tenant synchronization relationship.|Restrict DC policy management and separate it from ordinary server administration.|A domain link or GPO read right does not prove effective DC configuration control.|T1484.001;T1556.007|AC-6;CM-3;CM-5|Protect policy changes that affect the source identity control plane.||High
002|A writable policy script executes on a hybrid bridge|An unapproved principal can modify a script or dependency referenced by an effective startup, logon, or policy execution path on a bridge AND the execution identity has sensitive rights.|Script path and ACL metadata; GPO/task reference; resultant application; execution identity; host role.|Protect referenced script files and their directories and remove unnecessary privileged execution.|Do not run or print script contents containing secrets. A dead reference or user-context script without useful rights is not host control.|T1484.001;T1059.001|CM-5;SI-7;AC-6|Protect the integrity of centrally invoked code and its privilege.||High
003|An unnecessary spooler increases exposure on a vulnerable hybrid host|Spooler is enabled on a DC or bridge without an approved need AND a specific applicable vendor advisory, patch state, and reachable interface establish a relevant exposure.|Service state; business exception; OS build/update inventory; exact vendor advisory applicability; approved reachability evidence.|Remove unnecessary print services and apply the supported security update through change control.|Service enabled alone is a posture issue, not proof of PrintNightmare or another exploit. Never probe exploitation.|T1210;T1068|CM-7;SI-2|Reduce unnecessary service exposure and remediate an applicable flaw.||High
004|A lower-trust operator can weaken bridge endpoint protection|A principal outside the approved boundary can change effective protection settings or exclusions for a bridge through GPO or management tooling.|Policy-owner path; effective protection settings; scoped exclusions; tamper-protection state; device management precedence.|Restrict protection-policy changes and remove unjustified broad exclusions.|A stale GPO setting may be overridden. Protection disabled by design for a validated equivalent product requires review, not automatic failure.|T1685|CM-5;SI-3;SI-4|Protect the configuration and coverage of preventive and monitoring tools.||High
005|A writable service or task runs with hybrid control-plane privilege|An unapproved principal can modify an executable, service configuration, or scheduled task whose effective run identity controls a hybrid host or identity.|Service/task DACL; executable and parent-directory ACL; run identity; enabled trigger; host role.|Restrict configuration and binary writes and remove unnecessary privileged run identities.|Path strings alone are insufficient. Quote handling, file existence, trigger state, and effective write permission matter.|T1543.003;T1053.005|CM-5;SI-7;AC-6|Protect privileged execution configuration and code integrity.||High
006|Guest or anonymous access has useful rights on a hybrid host|A bridge accepts an enabled Guest or anonymous authentication path AND its effective resource or logon authorization exposes sensitive access.|Guest SID state; effective authentication policy; resource ACL; network scope; host role.|Disable unnecessary guest paths and remove sensitive anonymous or guest grants.|An enabled Guest account does not prove remote access; local and network deny rights must be evaluated.|T1078.003|AC-2;IA-2;AC-3|Require identified authorized access to hybrid infrastructure.||High
007|Weak source password policy aligns with weak cloud sign-in protection|A privileged synchronized password identity is governed by a password policy below the approved requirement AND effective cloud authentication lacks the specified independent protection.|Resultant fine-grained/domain policy; identity mapping; password authority; active privilege; applicable CA and SCuBA evidence.|Improve source password policy and the applicable independent cloud authentication control.|Policy metadata is not password strength measurement. A tenant-level MFA failure is not automatically applicable to this account.|T1110;T1078.004|IA-5;IA-2;AC-6|Protect the same privileged identity at source and cloud authentication boundaries.|MS-CA;SCUBA-AAD|High
008|An unsupported or unpatched bridge remains on a sensitive administrative route|A confirmed bridge has a vendor-verified unsupported or applicable unpatched component AND an administrative or service route exposes that component within the assessed threat boundary.|Exact component/version; current vendor lifecycle or advisory; update inventory; service exposure; bridge responsibility.|Move to a supported version and remediate applicable flaws with a tested recovery plan.|Unsupported status is not an exploit. Distinguish lifecycle risk from a confirmed applicable vulnerability and do not invent CVEs.|T1210;T1068|SI-2;CM-8;RA-5|Track identity infrastructure components and prioritize applicable flaws by their role.||High
